<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan's State Oil up 1.76 percent.</title>
<headline>Pakistan's State Oil up 1.76 percent.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan State Oil Co Ltd (PSO) jumped six rupees, or 1.76 percent, to 347 on Thursday on expectations of good company results, dealers said.</p>
<p>By midsession, some 14,600 shares were traded.</p>
<p>&quot;PSO is a blue-chip company and people expect it to announce good results at its board meeting on November 3,&quot; dealer Shakil Anwar said.</p>
<p>PSO has already announced an interim dividend of 30 percent.</p>
<p>Dealers said the recent 7.86 percent devaluation of the rupee against the dollar and 10 percent rise in petroleum prices would further increase PSO's profits.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
